# Generated by `next dev` / `next build`, never edited by hand, and **rewritten to a different
# value depending on which command ran**: `next dev` writes `.next/dev/types/...` while
# `next build` writes `.next/types/...`. Committing it therefore produced a one-line diff every
# time a dev server and a build alternated — noise in every `git status`, and a change with no
# reviewable content.
#
# Verified safe to ignore rather than assumed: `tsc --noEmit` (the first CI step, which runs
# before `next build`, on a clone with no `.next/` and no `next-env.d.ts`) passes, and
# `next dev` / `next build` regenerate the file themselves.
next-env.d.ts

